+# To-Do app
+
+A minimal local to-do app matching the stack in PROJECT_CONFIG.md: a single static page, no build step, no server, no runtime dependencies.
+
+## Files
+
+- `index.html` — markup and styles. Loads `app.js` as a module.
+- `app.js` — all logic. `createTodoStore(storage)` is the storage-backed store; `initTodoApp({ document, storage })` wires it to the DOM; the module self-initializes when a `#todo-form` exists.
+- `test/todo.test.js` — executable checks (`node --test` + jsdom, dev-only).
+
+## Behavior
+
+- **Add:** `store.add(text)` trims input and returns `null` for blank/whitespace-only text; the UI then shows "Enter a task before adding." and adds nothing.
+- **Complete/incomplete:** `store.toggle(id)` flips the `completed` flag.
+- **Delete:** `store.remove(id)` removes one task.
+- **Persistence:** tasks live in `localStorage` under `todo.tasks.v1`. Corrupted JSON and malformed entries are ignored rather than thrown, so a reload never bricks the page.
+
+Task text is rendered with `textContent`, so stored text cannot inject markup.
+
+## Checks
+
+```
+pnpm install
+pnpm test
+```
+
+`test/todo.test.js` mounts the real `index.html` in jsdom, wires the real `app.js`, and drives it through form submit, checkbox change, and delete clicks. It covers add/trim, blank rejection, toggle both ways, targeted delete, persistence across a simulated reload (same `localStorage`, fresh DOM), corrupted storage, and malformed entries.
+
+## Verification notes
+
+- `pnpm test` → 7 passed, 0 failed (Node v26.3.0, jsdom 30.1.1).
+- Reload is simulated by re-mounting a fresh DOM seeded with the previous `localStorage` snapshot; real browser reload was not exercised.
+- No visual/browser rendering was checked (no browser available in this environment).
